{"reference":"Ezekiel 14","book":"Ezekiel","chapter":14,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Job in Ezekiel","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"By naming Job alongside Noah and Daniel as a righteous figure, Ezekiel 14 treats him as a recognized example of righteousness. That use does not, by itself, decide whether the completed book of Job should be read as modern-style biography or as pure fiction; its prose setting, poetic dialogues, literary artistry, and ancient reception need to be considered separately.","verse_refs":["Ezekiel 14:14","Ezekiel 14:20"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_ezekiel_014_41e7ddc2c0d779269816693b"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}